# Qt

**Color:** `#4A9EFF` | **Nodes:** 10

The Qt category provides nodes for interacting with the Qt framework — connecting signals, reading/writing QObject properties, invoking methods, and responding to widget and QML events.

## QObject

**Color:** `#4A9EFF`

| Type | Node Name | Inputs | Outputs | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `qt/qobject/connectSignal` | Connect Signal | sender(String), signal(String), receiver(String), slot(String) | connected(Bool) | Wire a Qt signal to a slot dynamically |
| `qt/qobject/emitSignal` | Emit Signal | signal(String), value(Generic) | emitted(Bool) | Emit a named Qt signal with a payload |
| `qt/qobject/setProperty` | Set Property | object(String), property(String), value(Generic) | success(Bool) | Set a QObject property by name |
| `qt/qobject/getProperty` | Get Property | object(String), property(String) | value(Generic) | Read a QObject property by name |
| `qt/qobject/invokeMethod` | Invoke Method | object(String), method(String), arg(Generic) | result(Generic) | Call a QObject method dynamically |

### Example Uses

```
"button1" "clicked" → [Connect Signal] → [Display]    // React to button click
"slider1" "value"  → [Get Property]   → [Number Display]  // Read slider value
[Object] [Method] → [Invoke Method]   → [Display]     // Call a method dynamically
```

## Widgets

**Color:** `#FF9F43`

| Type | Node Name | Inputs | Outputs | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `qt/widgets/buttonClicked` | Button Clicked | text(String) | clicked(Bool) | Fires when a button with matching text is clicked |
| `qt/widgets/sliderValue` | Slider Value | min(Float), max(Float), value(Float) | value(Float) | Read/control a slider widget |
| `qt/widgets/textChanged` | Text Changed | text(String) | text(String) | Fires when text input changes |

### Example Uses

```
"Start" → [Button Clicked] → [Gate]                   // Trigger on button press
[0] [100] [50] → [Slider Value] → [Gauge]             // Control gauge with slider
[Text Field] → [Text Changed] → [String Concat]       // React to text input
```

## QML

**Color:** `#00CEC9`

| Type | Node Name | Inputs | Outputs | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `qt/qml/qmlProperty` | QML Property | objectId(String), property(String) | value(Generic) | Read a property from a QML object by ID |
| `qt/qml/qmlSignal` | QML Signal | objectId(String), signal(String) | value(Generic) | Connect to a QML signal by object ID |

### Example Uses

```
"myCanvas" "width" → [QML Property] → [Number Display]   // Monitor QML canvas width
"myButton" "clicked" → [QML Signal] → [Toggle]           // React to QML button click
```
